Hi all,

Using distance sampling in R (package Distance) we are trying to generate a population estimate of a particular bird for a particular island "A". However, we do not have enough detections to generate a detection function so we have pooled observations with a prior survey of a neighboring island "B". The problem is, for whatever reason the data were binned "Island A" (the one for which we desire the estimate) but not for the other island. We tried to bin all the data but are unable to get a good detection model fit. What we thought we would try is to generate the detection function with the survey data that are not-binned i.e. "Island B", for which we do get a good fit,  and then use that detection function to estimate abundance of new "Island A". Is this approach possible or valid? If so, can anyone offer a suggestion as to how one would supply a detection function generated with a different observation data set to my current dataset of interest with package Distance?

Thanks in advance,
